# mbsync (isync) config for Gmail, shared by every mail host.
# Install: cd ~/dotfiles && stow mbsync
#
# The password is never in this repo.  Each machine keeps its Gmail app
# password in ~/.config/mbsync/gmail-password (mode 600, no newline).
# See README.md in this module.

IMAPAccount gmail
Host imap.gmail.com
User jclosure@gmail.com
PassCmd "cat ~/.config/mbsync/gmail-password"
AuthMechs LOGIN
# SSLType works on isync 1.4 (Ubuntu) and 1.5 (Homebrew); 1.5 also calls it
# TLSType.  No CertificateFile: use the system CA store on each OS.
SSLType IMAPS

IMAPStore gmail-remote
Account gmail

MaildirStore gmail-local
Subfolders Verbatim
Path ~/Mail/
Inbox ~/Mail/Inbox

Channel gmail
Far :gmail-remote:
Near :gmail-local:
# Every folder, [Gmail]/All Mail included: archived mail lives only there,
# and it is mu4e's refile (archive) folder.  (The old line here,
# `Patterns * ![Gmail]/All Mail', meant to skip it, but patterns split on
# spaces, so it excluded a nonexistent "[Gmail]/All" and synced everything.
# To really skip All Mail, quote it: Patterns * "![Gmail]/All Mail".)
Patterns *
Create Near
SyncState *
# Actually remove messages flagged deleted, on both sides.  Without this a
# message trashed on one machine stays on the others with only the Trashed
# flag (mu4e shows it struck through), forever.  mu4e's trash doesn't set
# that flag (see emacs-ide init.el, "Gmail-safe trash"), so this never
# removes mail that is merely in Trash; Gmail purges that after 30 days.
Expunge Both
